# --- Provider (Cline SDK) -------------------------------------------------
# ANY provider id in the SDK registry works — there are ~230, not just Anthropic.
# List them all (with the exact key variable and default model) via:
#     npm run dev -- --list-providers
# Examples: anthropic | deepseek | groq | openai-native | gemini | xai | mistral
#           | openrouter | together | cerebras | fireworks | ollama | lmstudio
YOUTUBE_INGEST_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Model. Leave commented out to use the provider's own default from the registry
# (deepseek -> deepseek-v4-flash, groq -> moonshotai/kimi-k2-instruct-0905, ...).
# YOUTUBE_INGEST_MODEL=

# API key for the chosen provider. Only ONE of these is needed — the variable
# name comes from the SDK registry, not from this file.
#   anthropic -> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   deepseek -> DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
#   groq      -> GROQ_API_KEY        xai      -> XAI_API_KEY
#   gemini    -> GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=

# --- Behaviour ------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute path to the Obsidian vault that source notes are written into.
YOUTUBE_INGEST_VAULT=/Users/elminnurkic/Documents/Second Brain
# Preferred transcript language (ISO 639-1). Leave EMPTY to prefer the video's
# original/English track. Setting e.g. "sv" only helps if the video actually has
# a Swedish track — otherwise YouTube may return an auto-translated track, which
# is machine-translated wording rather than what was actually said. Choose
# deliberately; empty is the safe default.
YOUTUBE_INGEST_LANG=
